  "question": {
    "text": "A body starts from rest on a long inclined plane of slope $45^{\\circ}$. The coefficient of friction between the body and the plane varies as $\\mu=0.3 x$, where $x$ is distance travelled down the plane. The body will have maximum speed (for $g=10 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}^2$ ) when $x=$",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "k0Ier",
      "text": "\n$9.8 \\mathrm{~m}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "CNuyh",
      "text": "\n$27 \\mathrm{~m}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "OLXSz",
      "text": "\n$12 \\mathrm{~m}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "d197k",
      "text": "\n$3.33 \\mathrm{~m}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "When the body has maximum speed then\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mu=0.3 \\mathrm{x}=\\tan 45^{\\circ} \\\\\n& \\therefore \\mathrm{x}=3.33 \\mathrm{~m}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
